Now I understand the flaky test. The get_recently_changed_files calls `git log --diff-filter=M --name-only --pretty=format: -n 20`, which only shows modified files. In CI, if the checkout has a shallow clone or the recently pushed commits only added new files (not modified), this could return empty and then the section wouldn't be present, causing the test to fail.

